---
description: Require exact file paths and line numbers in code guidance
alwaysApply: true
---

# File and line references

- When explaining where to add, remove, or change code, always identify the exact file path and current line number.
- Include a clickable file link when the interface supports it.
- Show the existing code and the replacement code when practical.
- If edits shift line numbers, state that the number is based on the current file contents.
- When the user asks a question, requests an explanation, or asks what should change, do not edit project code automatically.
- For question-style requests, inspect read-only and explain the exact file, current line, proposed code, and reason.
- Edit project code only when the user explicitly asks to apply, implement, modify, fix, or otherwise make the change.
